  "notes": "Vulnerable isPrivateOrLocalHostname() (urlSafety.ts:95) lowercases and trims but never strips brackets, so isIP('[::1]') is 0 and the literal passes; same bracketed-IPv6 miss for any [::ffff:x] or [fe80::] literal. The fix strips brackets and delegates range checks to ipaddr.js. The advisory also cites non-resolving hosts; fix version 2.1.7. Patched file notes the authoritative boundary moved to request-filtering-agent in src/utils/httpRequest.ts (connect-time re-validation, not vendored here).",
